Travelling landings only (2026-11-24, the cooldown-clock round): the placement's event rule (logcasts.ts
eventStopStart) for an ultimate whose first landing travels (KitHit.travels, from LaunchProjectile), without the
check that its frame's stop covers a teammate's logged hit, and for no other detached landing.

Measured (with burst-stops `others`): the same placements for every projectile ultimate as the old rule, with or
without the check; 3aa6 plain 396 -> 397 (Arclight's dash, an ability entity, from its frame). Dropped: with
burst-stops `all` b7b3 (verified) plain 47 -> 45, Tangtang's stare (an ability entity, launch 76) from its frame
moves Arcane's 10.34 s burst off. Kept instead: travelling landings always from their event, other detached ones
under the check (the old rule; the same numbers as before).

Would work if: ability entities that move (Tangtang's stare, Arclight's dash) had a field of their own, from data
that says whether the entity flies to the target.

The diff is against the commit before b03189c (apply with --at b03189c~1).

